title: 'pallet-revive: benchmark some EVM arithmetic op-codes'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet-revive` now charges the EVM `DIV`, `SDIV`, `MOD`, `SMOD`, `ADDMOD` and `MULMOD`
    op-codes from their own benchmarks. All other EVM op-codes and all PVM instructions keep their
    current charges.

    `pallet_revive::WeightInfo` has seven new methods, each taking the number of op-codes executed:

    - `evm_pop_opcode`
    - `evm_div_opcode`
    - `evm_sdiv_opcode`
    - `evm_mod_opcode`
    - `evm_smod_opcode`
    - `evm_addmod_opcode`
    - `evm_mulmod_opcode`

    The arithmetic op-codes are benchmarked in pairs with a `POP`. Their charge is the slope of
    their benchmark minus the slope of `evm_pop_opcode`. `POP` itself is still charged as before.

    Runtimes that use `pallet_revive::weights::SubstrateWeight` or `()` need no changes. Runtimes
    with their own `WeightInfo` implementation stop compiling until they implement the new methods.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    In EVM contracts, `DIV`, `SDIV`, `MOD`, `SMOD`, `ADDMOD` and `MULMOD` use a different amount
    of gas than before. Results and all other behavior are unchanged, and deployed contracts don't
    need to be redeployed. PVM contracts are not affected.

    Estimate gas with `eth_estimateGas` instead of reusing gas limits recorded before this change.
    Contracts that pass a fixed gas amount to calls into code that runs these op-codes should check
    that the amount is still enough.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: major
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
